{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeRQrk9PCmsAXj4YPojN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the 8 test statistics to `iter_0/critique/test_stats/`. I ran each one once on the observed responses: each returned a finite number in a few milliseconds, far under the 0.3 s budget per call. I didn't run the posterior-predictive check — the pipeline does that — so there are no p-values yet.\n\nThe incumbent model gives every participant the same parameters and treats each trial as independent. It also scores sequences only by multiscale balance, the alternation rate and periodicity. Each statistic below targets one of those simplifications:\n\n| Statistic | What it probes | Observed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `participant_alternation_pref_sd` | How much people differ in how often they pick the more-alternating sequence (the model has no per-person differences) | 0.160 |\n| `pair_choice_extremity` | How close to unanimous people are on each pair, i.e. whether the model's predictions are too confident or too weak | 0.251 |\n| `shorter_run_rate_matched_alternations` | Whether people avoid long streaks once the alternation count is held equal | 0.588 |\n| `balance_rate_matched_alternations` | Whether people prefer the sequence with a more even H/T count once the alternation count is held equal (the model averages balance across window sizes, which may dilute this) | 0.613 |\n| `perfect_alternation_choice_rate` | How often a perfectly alternating sequence (HTHT…) is chosen | 0.634 |\n| `high_alternation_preference` | Which way people lean when both sequences already alternate a lot (tests where the model's ideal alternation rate sits) | 0.573 |\n| `alternation_pref_drift_over_trials` | Whether the preference for alternation shifts between the first and second half of a session (the model can't change over time) | −0.020 |\n| `same_side_perseveration` | Whether people keep clicking the same side as on their previous trial | 0.494 |\n\nEach file's `# description:` says which direction of difference from the model's predictions counts as a failure, so the next round can read it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":612,"cache_read_input_tokens":49739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":612,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":673,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c891e1c9-ee00-4f5f-92c7-10101418f968","uuid":"209ef974-b9bf-47a6-92e8-01aeca477735","timestamp":"2026-10-03T01:17:38.910Z","request_id":"req_011CfeRQrLLbXSjMZivtR2xv"}
